Software Foundation — command reference

Native prerequisites: CMake >=3.24, Ninja, C++20 compiler, Python >=3.9.
No configuration or normal build downloads or installs software.

./build.sh                                      # incremental Debug build
./build.sh test dev --label core --jobs 2        # smallest core group
./build.sh test dev --label tools --jobs 2       # development-tool contracts
./build.sh test release --full --jobs 2          # all enabled local tests
./build.sh test asan --full --jobs 2             # GCC/Clang instrumentation
./build.sh package release --jobs 2             # native archive; not certification

Windows developer prompt: replace ./build.sh with python tools/build.py.
GUI: ./build.sh test dev --gui-source /absolute/pinned/gui-boundary --label gui
SDK: ./build.sh build release --sdk /absolute/prepared-sdk --jobs 2
Wasm: ./build.sh test release --sdk /absolute/browser-sdk --gui-source /absolute/pinned/gui-boundary --gui-backends wasm --label gui
Browser Release retains assertions and exceptions to match the prepared frozen cache.
The same SDK can test core/CLI contracts under retained Node without GUI inputs:
./build.sh test release --sdk /absolute/browser-sdk --gui-backends wasm --label core --build-dir build/wasm-core
These use separate build/dev-gui and build/release-sdk directories.

Direct CMake (also supports generators other than Ninja):
cmake --preset dev
cmake --build build/dev --target foundation-tests --parallel 2
ctest --test-dir build/dev --output-on-failure --no-tests=error --parallel 2
cmake --install build/release --prefix /absolute/staging-prefix

Visual Studio and Ninja Multi-Config require --config Release for build/install,
-C Release for CTest and -C Release for CPack. See docs/building.md.
Do not run tests from a stale build tree or assume CTest compiles prerequisites.
See docs/testing.md, docs/sdk.md and docs/portability.md for scope and prerequisites.
